<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58109" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνά̆φ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>prickly teasel</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alc.Com.
				35
			</span></i>; used by fullers to card or clean cloth, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				166
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱπποφαές</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.106
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>carding-comb</i>, also used as an instrument of torture, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ κνάφου ἕλκειν τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.92
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κναφηΐον</span> codd.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				2.114
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.858e
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γναφ</span>-), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
